Subject: [PATCH 1/3] ci: make contract-check a blocking gate
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The keeper-wire drift that kept `contract-check` report-only is resolved
upstream and already re-pinned here:

- door-kit#21 (client sends `ledgerRef`, keeperd reads `manifestDigest`):
  the agreement was corrected — keeper-wire bc59436 declares `ledgerRef`
  for import-and-push (trellis #16 re-pinned it + skips `kind`).
- door-keeper#15 (stale vendored door-kit client): door-keeper cd370da
  re-synced lib/{keeper,runtime}.ts to door-kit HEAD (trellis #17
  re-pinned it → door-kit-mirror byte-identical).

At the current flake.lock pins every check `nix flake check` runs is
green (keeper-wire, scout-wire, concierge-wire, door-kit-mirror,
sanctioned-reader-seam, descriptor-honesty, lattice — the signed
`status` branch built from main 40ec246 records the same), so the
report-only escape hatch only hides real drift now.

- .github/workflows/ci.yml: drop `continue-on-error: true` from
  `contract-check`; the job comment now describes a blocking gate.
- flake.nix / README.md: retire the comments and prose that still
  described keeper-wire, door-kit-mirror and lattice as red / report-only,
  drop the reference to the removed specs/keeper-wire.json from the
  keeper-wire check comment, and bring the README status table up to the
  seven verified types in registry.ts (adds concierge-wire and
  descriptor-honesty).

No check logic changes.

Closes #2

